From ffbbcf047af59238b9518915fb9a112481e3b98b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: logdog2325 <loganjayfisher@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 00:27:50 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] GBA link: full-boot presence cycling + dithered cadence,
 armed-rescue, roll instrumentation

Session forensics against the first fully-instrumented successful battle
settled the last failure mode: whenever XD actually asked, the GBA
answered and the whole flow ran (arm -> ladder -> upload -> client ->
both sockets -> battle); in the failed sessions XD never sent a byte.
The game's detection is armed by the player's own menu navigation and
then samples GBA presence -- and the previous reset cadence kept the GBA
visible only ~12% of the time in short BIOS beacons, with a cycle length
of exactly 65.0000 video frames, so a frame-grid sampler could stay
phase-locked out of every window for an entire session.

Fix, in three parts. (1) Full-boot presence cycling (GBA/FullBootPresence,
default on): raise the minimum reset spacing to 5 s so every boot runs
past the BIOS beacons into Emerald's long cartridge window -- the one the
JoyBoot ladder needs -- before the falling-edge trigger fires at its
close. Observed cycle ~7.8-8.2 s with ~41% presence duty, every cycle
armable. Spacings between 3.45 and 4.79 s would reset in the dead gap
before that window and silently recreate the starved regime; documented
so nobody picks one. (2) A deterministic 0-450 ms dither on the edge
debounce, derived from the reset ordinal, so consecutive cycles never
repeat a length and no sampler can stay phase-locked; pure function of
synced state, ordinal-global so both sockets stay in phase. (3) An
armed-rescue clause: if XD arms on the cartridge window's last moments
and loses it mid-ladder, the established latch used to wedge the socket
against further resets; release it after the link has been down 0.5 s
with 8 s since our reset and reboot through the same synced path.

Instrumentation for whatever remains: A/B/Start rising edges from the GC
pad logged on the detect-log clock (every detection roll timestamped
against window state), a policy line at session start, ord=/dither= on
every reset. On-screen fallback rule after 60 s unlinked and a launcher
tip: back out with B and re-enter VS mode -- each entry is a fresh roll.

Also register GBADetectLog in DolphinLib.props: the Windows build links
the SI/GBA objects that now call it, and would have failed at link.
